      nursingEssentials: ["Before initiation or dose escalation, assess pressure, orthostasis, volume status, creatinine/eGFR, potassium, pregnancy potential, NSAID/diuretic exposure, potassium products, and whether renal perfusion may be RAAS dependent.", "After a start or dose change, trend creatinine and potassium rather than treating one value in isolation. A modest early eGFR dip can reflect the intended efferent-arteriole effect; a large or progressive decline should trigger review for volume depletion, NSAIDs, renal-artery stenosis, sepsis, obstruction, or excessive pressure reduction."],
