      contraindications: ["Pregnancy; previous ACE-inhibitor-related angioedema; hereditary or idiopathic angioedema for many labels; and use with sacubitril/valsartan or within its required 36-hour separation.", "Do not combine aliskiren with an ACE inhibitor in diabetes. Clarify severe hyperkalemia, symptomatic hypotension, evolving AKI, or suspected bilateral renal-artery stenosis before giving."],
      nursingEssentials: ["Identify the specific ACE inhibitor, indication, formulation, and renal dosing. Check pressure, orthostasis, volume, potassium, creatinine/eGFR, cough, facial/tongue swelling, pregnancy status, and interacting drugs.", "Teach that lip, tongue, throat, or facial swelling is an airway emergency and can occur even after long exposure. A dry cough is not an allergy, but it may require a class change after other causes are considered."],
