      keyLabs: ["Baseline and follow-up creatinine/eGFR and potassium, blood pressure/orthostasis, volume status, urine albumin when kidney protection is the target, and CBC when collagen-vascular disease or neutropenia risk is relevant.", "Evaluate a major creatinine rise by checking volume loss, pressure, NSAIDs, diuretics, sepsis, obstruction, and renal-artery disease rather than reflexively calling all changes nephrotoxicity."],
      nclexTraps: ["The -pril ending identifies the class, but not identical dosing or indications. Captopril food timing, enalaprilat IV use, and fosinopril elimination are agent-specific.", "ACE-inhibitor angioedema is often bradykinin mediated, so absence of hives does not make tongue swelling safe and ordinary allergy treatment may not rapidly reverse the airway threat."],
