      contraindications: ["Do not combine ACE inhibitor with ARNI or start one within 36 hours of the other. Avoid ARNI and ACE inhibitors in any relevant angioedema history according to guideline and labeling.", "Do not stack ACE inhibitor plus ARB or add aliskiren in diabetes. Pregnancy is a contraindication to direct RAAS blockade."],
      nursingEssentials: ["When switching, identify the previous drug and last dose. The 36-hour rule applies specifically between ACE inhibitor and sacubitril/valsartan because of overlapping peptide metabolism; it is not an arbitrary scheduling preference.", "Trend pressure, potassium, creatinine, volume, cough, swelling, and clinical outcome. Check whether the card's indication is evidence-based for that exact drug and condition."],
